// texel, which makes the stencil lopsided; on a sloped plane (the terrace floor) that leaves a non-zero Laplacian in
// big moire-shaped patches that read as grey arches and swirls. The fractional line thickness is kept by blending the
// Laplacians at the two whole-texel spacings around it: each one is exactly zero on any plane.
